WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.483
Is a place a town

2
00:00:01.483 --> 00:00:02.696
or a village?

3
00:00:02.696 --> 00:00:03.863
The census has its own

4
00:00:03.863 --> 00:00:05.328
test, and it's stricter than

5
00:00:05.328 --> 00:00:06.408
you think.

6
00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:07.783
In 2011,

7
00:00:07.783 --> 00:00:10.661
31.1 percent of Indians lived

8
00:00:10.661 --> 00:00:12.509
in urban areas.

9
00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:15.201
Up from about 27.8 percent

10
00:00:15.201 --> 00:00:16.609
in 2001.

11
00:00:16.951 --> 00:00:18.760
At least five thousand people.

12
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.435
At least 75 percent of

13
00:00:20.435 --> 00:00:22.746
working men outside farming.

14
00:00:22.746 --> 00:00:23.936
And a density of at

15
00:00:23.936 --> 00:00:25.549
least 400 people per square

16
00:00:25.549 --> 00:00:26.660
kilometre.

17
00:00:27.005 --> 00:00:28.888
Many census towns are still

18
00:00:28.888 --> 00:00:30.431
run by panchayats.

19
00:00:30.431 --> 00:00:31.643
That gap shows up in

20
00:00:31.643 --> 00:00:33.984
water, sanitation and planning.

21
00:00:34.673 --> 00:00:35.850
Your turn.

22
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.079
Which is not a criterion?
